; expr-env: one binding per row, plus a vec3 that packs three of them. With
; :dur 2bar the dur binding is 8 beats (not seconds), bpm is the document
; tempo, and t is the host clock in seconds. `phase` is the 0..1 position
; inside the current bar, the same value :emit [phase] would broadcast.
(transport :bpm 120 :meter [4 4] :dur 2bar)

(track :target ticks :expr tick)
(track :target grid :expr [beat bar phase])
(track :target rate :expr (* bpm dur))
(track :target seconds :expr t)
